#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/images-and-video/en.mdx:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Blob objects\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/images-and-video/en.mdx:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blobs are authoritatively stored by the account's PDS instance, but views are commonly served by CDNs associated with individual applications (\"AppViews\"), to reduce traffic on the PDS. CDNs may serve transformed (resized, transcoded, etc) versions of the original blob.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/images-and-video/en.mdx:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "While blobs are universally content addressed (by CID), they are always referenced and managed in the context of an individual account (DID).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/images-and-video/en.mdx:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "The empty blob (zero bytes) is valid in general, though it may be disallowed by individual Lexicons/applications.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/images-and-video/en.mdx:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "Creating blobs requires the permission scope **`blob:*/*` .**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/images-and-video/en.mdx:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is generally recommended to use an object storage implementation for working with blobs if you are hosting your own PDS. See [going to production](/guides/going-to-production#object-storage) for more.\n"
msgstr ""

